      "canonical_isomeric_smiles": "N=C(N)NCCCCN",
      "citation": "Agmatine (4-aminobutylguanidine), CAS 306-60-5, C5H14N4, MW 130.19. ADVERSARIAL over-exclusion probe: a molecule with a real, structurally remote primary amine (terminal butyl -NH2, 2 H's, attached to a plain CH2 carbon far from the guanidine carbon) COEXISTING with an incidental guanidine group elsewhere in the same molecule. The R-N02 fix must exclude only the N-H atoms whose OWN attached carbon bears the C=N bond (the guanidine's own 3 N's), not collaterally zero out unrelated amine N-H elsewhere in the molecule. Not tested by R-N02, its refuting receipts, or any other novel probe in this verify -- every other probe here has zero non-guanidine N-H, so none could catch a too-broad, whole-molecule exclusion bug. Pre-registered refute trigger: observed reactive_amine_hydrogen_count != 2 or observed_role != hardener.",
